invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_mul.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_digit
reason: a window's digit takes its sign from the window's own top bit,
  bit 4i + 3, where the recoding takes it from the bit above the window,
  bit 4i + 4. The digits then no longer add up to k | 1.
  proof/p256_wide_digit_harness.c proves that sum for every 256-bit k,
  where a vector holds it for the scalars it carries. Each run is a
  proof, so this belongs to the nightly's test-invariants-proof-backed
  job.

--- old
        positive = scalar_bit(k, low + WINDOW_BITS);
--- new
        positive = scalar_bit(k, low + WINDOW_BITS - 1);
